# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files listed here are never saved into git, so they can never be uploaded to
# GitHub by accident. This is separate from what Claude can see: Claude's rules
# live in .claude/settings.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The private/ folder: ignore everything in it except the two template files
private/*
!private/README.md
!private/TEST-SECRET.txt

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets/
credentials.json

# Your personal Claude Code overrides for this project (not meant to be shared)
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Backups you make before editing the settings. Keep them on disk, out of git.
.claude/settings.json.backup
.claude/*.backup
*-backup.json

# Operating system clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor clutter
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Common build output and downloaded packages
node_modules/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Logs
*.log

# Cached web responses from the tools in tools/ (safe to delete at any time)
tools/.cache/

# The AI-use log is your own working record, not part of this template, so none
# of its contents are committed here. The folder and its README are tracked so a
# fresh copy knows what goes there; everything written into it is yours.
#
# Using this template for a real project and want your own logs in git? Delete
# the three lines below.
workspace/ai-use-log/.last-logged-commit
workspace/ai-use-log/sessions/
workspace/ai-use-log/DISCLOSURE.md

# Literature reviews are your own work, not part of this template, so none of a
# review folder is committed here. That covers both the downloaded papers, which
# are other people's copyrighted work and mostly not redistributable, and the
# summaries and reference files, which belong to whoever ran the review.
#
# Using this template for a real project and want your reviews in git? Delete the
# line below, and add back a rule for the papers themselves:
#     workspace/Literature_Review_*/**/*.pdf
#     workspace/Literature_Review_*/**/*_fulltext.txt
workspace/Literature_Review_*/
